{
  "version": "holdout-v1",
  "description": "Held-out Spanish (Peru-leaning) conversations, never used to tune prompts or thresholds. Score here only after changes tuned on dataset.v1.json are frozen. Neither provider's output is ground truth.",
  "labelingGuide": [
    "Label what the CUSTOMER expresses in the visible messages; BUSINESS messages are context only.",
    "Signals describe the customer's current state across the window; a signal reversed by a later customer message (cancellation undone, objection resolved) is not labeled.",
    "AVAILABILITY_REQUESTED = asks if a slot/stock exists; BOOKING_INTENT = commits to or accepts a slot.",
    "OBJECTION = concern while still considering; NO_LONGER_INTERESTED = explicit decline/cancel/withdrawal in the latest stance.",
    "QUOTE_REQUESTED = custom estimate for the customer's need; a single list-price question is PRICING_REQUESTED.",
    "acceptableIntents / acceptableInterestLevels list every label a reviewer considers correct when the case is genuinely ambiguous; expected.* is the preferred one.",
    "Set review.status to 'reviewed' (with reviewer and date) only after a human has checked the labels; the runner scores reviewed cases only unless --include-drafts is passed."
  ],
